 "code_head_note": "Measured at `e9a572d4b499d52050ee29bd2a8bf6cb0ab67134`, which the #12304 rebases rewrote OUT of every ref (it is a dangling local object, absent from a fresh clone), so the field names the latest rebased stand-in instead. EQUIVALENCE IS SCOPED, not global: `git diff e9a572d4b4 ae63e846e410 -- tortoise/entity_resolver.py tortoise/entity_blocking.py tortoise/extractor_v2.py` is EMPTY \u2014 those three files are the code this measurement exercises, and on them the two commits are identical (`git patch-id` agrees). The commit is NOT globally identical to the pre-rebase one \u2014 the whole tree diff is 89 files (`git diff --shortstat e9a572d4b4 ae63e846e410` -> `89 files changed, 25197 insertions(+), 794 deletions(-)`), which is just the base moving under it. Changes to those three files AFTER ae63e846e410: `5b618ed0524d` moved the `emitted:` docstring (no statement, no call); `f546f0e5a957` added the `complete=True` note; `d52a989eafd2` renamed the `lsh_bands` docstring label and the `stats()` counter key `keys`->`key_memberships` \u2014 a LABEL change to a diagnostic dict, with the counter's value and every attach decision unchanged. `22ec4d1a6048` then added a `candidates(label=None)` LABEL FALLBACK \u2014 the LAST statement change in these three files, i.e. the only one AFTER `d52a989eaf` \u2014 and this run never reaches it: the harness calls `index.candidates(surface, label=\"Object\")` (the variant arm of `run()`, in `tools/candidate_recall_11901.py`), so the `label is None` branch is not taken. Renamed from `keys` in `index_stats` in `d52a989eaf`: the counter increments once per (member, block) pair, so 10968 is key MEMBERSHIPS across 1000 members, not 10968 distinct keys (the index has 8449 blocks). \u26d4 The list is a SNAPSHOT at this artifact's head, and a docstring-only commit landed after it is NOT named above (the round-7 residual declaration in `entity_blocking.py`'s invariant 3 is one) \u2014 that does not weaken the claim. \u26d4 The claim about commits AFTER `ae63e846e410` is NOT what the `git diff` above proves: that compares two fixed commits and says nothing about anything later. It is re-proved by ENUMERATING them and comparing docstring-stripped ASTs per commit \u2014 `git log --format=%h ae63e846e410..HEAD -- tortoise/entity_resolver.py tortoise/entity_blocking.py tortoise/extractor_v2.py` -> the commits listed by that command, of which exactly TWO are statement changes: `d52a989eafd2` (the `stats()` key rename `keys` -> `key_memberships`, a diagnostic LABEL \u2014 which is why this artifact's field reads `key_memberships` while the run that produced it emitted `keys`) and `22ec4d1a6048` (the `candidates(label=None)` fallback, which this run never reaches). Every other commit on that list is docstring/comment-only. \u26d4 THE SCOPE ABOVE IS THE PRODUCT CODE, AND IT IS NOT THE WHOLE STORY \u2014 the code that PRODUCES this artifact is the harness `tools/candidate_recall_11901.py`, and it moved between the run and `code_head`: `git diff --stat e9a572d4b4 ae63e846e410 -- tools/candidate_recall_11901.py` is `494 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)` \u2014 the #12294 name-entropy arms came in with the base move. So a re-run AT `code_head` emits SIX arms this artifact does not contain: `gate`, `gate_by_class`, `gate_gated_names`, `gate_variant`, `pooled_coverage`, `pooled_gate`, every one an unconditional `arms[...] = ...` assignment in today's harness (16 assigned there vs the 10 held here: blocking / duplicate_rate / exact* / pooled / variant*). \u26d4 ENUMERATE that set, never grep for a couple of names \u2014 `grep -c 'gate_variant\\|pooled_gate'` reads 0 at `git show e9a572d4b4:tools/candidate_recall_11901.py` and 7 at `ae63e846e410`, which is how an earlier cut of this note undercounted the set by four and then asserted \"no gate arms\" beside a harness that assigns `arms[\"gate\"]`. The check is `git show <code_head>:tools/candidate_recall_11901.py | grep -o 'arms\\[\"[a-z_]*\"\\]' | sort -u` against this artifact's own `arms` keys. \u26d4 READ THIS AS THE REPRODUCTION CONTRACT: these numbers are the RUN's, produced by the harness as it stood at `e9a572d4b4`; re-running at `code_head` reproduces the ARMS this artifact holds (blocking, duplicate_rate, exact*, pooled, variant*) but emits those six EXTRA arms whose absence here is the base having moved, not a lost measurement. Re-running the #12294 arms is a separate run and is committed separately (`measurement-entropy-gate-12294.json`).",
